        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A mixture of H4BSC4A (43 mg, 0.05 mmol), NdCl3·6H2O (100 mg, 0.28 mmol), and MePO3H2 (5 mg, 0.05 mmol) in 2 mL CH3OH and 2 mL DMF was sealed in a 25 mL Teflon-lined bomb at 120 °C for 72 h, then cooled at 4 °C h−1 to room temperature. Colorless block-shaped crystals of 1 were isolated by filtration, washed with DMF/CH3OH (1:1, v/v) and air dried.",
