      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "Solid-state NIR luminescence at room temperature shows characteristic Nd(III) bands at 889, 1063 and 1327 nm, strongest at 1063 nm. DC magnetic data (2–300 K, 1000 Oe) give χmT = 15.92 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K, decreasing to 5.79 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Curie–Weiss fit (100–300 K) yields C = 16.05 cm3 K mol−1 and θ = −50.82 K, consistent with antiferromagnetic interactions and/or depopulation of Nd(III) Stark sublevels.",
